## Key Takeaways

- Abstract Data Types (ADTs) provide a clear specification of the operations on data, focusing on what the data does rather than how it is implemented.
- Common ADTs include Lists, Stacks, Queues, Sets, and Maps, each serving unique purposes.
- Utilizing Java's Collections Framework streamlines implementation and enhances code efficiency.
- Understanding the performance characteristics of various ADTs helps in making informed decisions during application development.

